    w: 1, title: "Why Defend the Faith? Introduction to Christian Apologetics", theme: "Christians are called to give reasons for their hope with gentleness and respect, to contend for the faith once delivered to the saints and to point people to Christ, not merely to win arguments",
    summary: "This opening lesson introduces apologetics, the reasoned defence of the Christian faith. First Peter 3:15 calls believers to be prepared to give a defence for the hope within them with gentleness and respect. Jude 3 urges contending for the faith. Acts 17:16-34 shows Paul reasoning in Athens. The lesson explains what apologetics is, why it matters, its limits, and outlines the course.",
    scripture: ["1 Peter 3:13-17", "Jude 3"], more: ["Acts 17:16-34", "Philippians 1:7", "2 Corinthians 10:4-5"], memory: "1 Peter 3:15",
