    summary: "Second Timothy 2:24-26 says the Lord's servant must not be quarrelsome but kind, patient, correcting opponents with gentleness in the hope that God may grant repentance. Colossians 4:5-6 calls for wisdom toward outsiders and gracious speech. Proverbs 15:1 and 18:13 teach gentle answers and listening. This lesson explores the virtues of the apologist, honesty with evidence, listening, and avoiding pride and manipulation.",
    scripture: ["2 Timothy 2:23-26", "Colossians 4:5-6"], more: ["Proverbs 15:1", "Proverbs 18:13", "James 1:19-20"], memory: "Colossians 4:6",
