    discuss: [
      ["Which lesson has helped you most so far?", "Invite short testimonies. Let learners answer in their own words and point back to the passage."],
      ["Which question or objection do you find most difficult?", "Share and note for future study. Give time for several answers before summarising from Scripture."],
      ["What skill do you want to develop?", "Listening, explaining or researching. Invite learners to support their answers from the passage studied."],
      ["How can we support one another in the second half?", "Prayer partners and study groups. Let learners answer in their own words and point back to the passage."],
    ],
    apply: "Complete the mid-course test honestly. Write two commitments for the second half. Review your memory verses and recite them to a friend. Share your plan with a trusted friend or family member this week and ask them to check in with you, then thank God for any progress.",
    activity: "Learners take the mid-course test under the teacher's supervision. Afterward discuss selected questions and review key passages. Close with prayer.",
